# ==============================================================================
# HyperDNS — Docker build context exclusions
# ==============================================================================
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies whatever the daemon does not exclude here,
# and what it copied before this file existed was the whole working tree: the
# master key that decrypts every subscriber record, the live encrypted database,
# the TLS private key, config.json with the admin credentials in it, and the four
# documents that are deliberately not published. All of that landed in a build
# layer. The final image only takes the binary out of the builder, but the layer
# itself is a real artefact — it sits in the build cache, it is what `docker
# build --target builder` produces, and a reseller who exports or pushes an
# intermediate image ships the key with it. One `.dockerignore` is the difference.
#
# Note on syntax: patterns here are matched against the *whole* relative path,
# not against each basename the way .gitignore does it. `*.key` matches only a
# key at the context root, which is why the secrets below are written `**/*.key`.
#
# Nothing that go:embed needs may be excluded, or the build fails at compile
# time: web/index.html, web/css/{style,portal}.css,
# web/js/{app,portal,tailwind,feather.min,chart.umd.min}.js and
# internal/version/version.json all have to reach the builder.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Cryptographic material — the master key is the whole database's confidentiality
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/master.key
**/master.key.bak
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
**/*.csr
**/*.cer
**/*.der
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
certs/
**/certs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Live state — a database, and the config that holds the admin credentials
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.bak
**/*.old
**/*.orig
config.json
config.local.json
config.dev.json
config.prod.json
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Documents that must never be published, in an image or anywhere else
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIVATE.md
STRUCTURE.md
CHANGELOG-PRIVATE.md
plan-testing.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Bulk the build has no use for. The context is uploaded to the daemon whole,
#    so every one of these is latency on every build.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/
.claude/
.remember/
_backup_v1.2/
offline-bundle/
dist/
bin/
build/
scratch/
_scratch/
t.sh
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# tailwind.min.css is 2.9 MB and is not one of the embedded assets — the binary
# reads web/js/tailwind.js instead. It is pure upload time.
web/css/tailwind.min.css

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Prebuilt binaries. A stale one copied in would be shadowed by the one this
#    build produces, but it is megabytes of context either way.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/*.out
hyperdns
hyperdns-*
hyperdns_*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Editor, OS and tooling noise
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.log
